orld Modeling: Visual Details Matter in Atari Paper List  Diffusion for World Modeling: Visual Details Matter in Atari\n Conference paper cited as reference [9] in AI for Games in the Foundation Model Era. In Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems, 2024.\n作者 Eloi Alonso, Adam Jelley, Vincent Micheli, Anssi Kanervisto, Amos Storkey, Tim Pearce, and François Fleuret\n发表年份 2024\n发表信息与来源 In Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems, 2024.\n发表类型 会议论文\n主要研究方向 玩家与世界建模\n研究方向 游玩与行动 玩家与世界建模\n研究主题 方向：世界与玩家建模 世界表征与持久状态 视频与学习式世界模型 方向：游玩与行动\n原始发表页面 原始发表页面 https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.12399 \nPDF PDF https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.12399 \narXiv ID 2405.12399\nDOI 10.48550/arxiv.2405.12399\n相关资源 DIAMOND — Diffusion for World Modeling /zh/resources/diamond/ \n书目来源 Survey reference [9] https://arxiv.org/html/2609.16679v1#bib.bib9  Primary publication https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.12399 \n综述中的引用位置 4.2 Representation, Uncertainty, and Persistent State https://arxiv.org/html/2609.16679v1#S4.SS2  9.1.2 Model Players and Games: World-Model Fidelity and Player-Model Validity https://arxiv.org/html/2609.16679v1#S9.SS1.SSS2  9.3.4 Reproducibility and Data Provenance https://arxiv.org/html/2609.16679v1#S9.SS3.SSS4  Appendix A System Index https://arxiv.org/html/2609.16679v1#A1 \n分类说明 Editorial roles and topics follow the survey’s cited sections and system index and the existing GameMap research notes. These are navigation categories, not independently verified capability claims.\n源码状态 开源代码\n代码仓库与许可证 eloialonso/diamond (implementation) 代码仓库 https://github.com/eloialonso/diamond 实现范围 研究实现 许可状态 开源许可证 代码许可 MIT License 许可证原文 https://github.com/eloialonso/diamond/blob/main/LICENSE\n项目主页 Project homepage https://diamond-wm.github.io \nDemo 与运行配置 Play the pretrained world model locally 体验入口 / 配置说明 https://github.com/eloialonso/diamond#readme 体验类型 有文档的本地运行入口 访问条件 需要本地配置 使用说明 Python, pretrained checkpoints and a compatible CUDA GPU are required; Atari and CS:GO use different documented setups.\n实际使用注意事项 MIT-licensed source and pretrained playable Atari/CS:GO world models are linked. Local interaction needs Python/model dependencies and a CUDA GPU; the project reports approximately 10 FPS on an RTX 3090 for the CS:GO setup. The external hosted link was reachable, but its execution was not independently playtested. A repository mentioning this paper was found through paper metadata, but author ownership or an official project-to-code link was not established. It is not counted as official source code. A project-linked demo endpoint was found, but a working interactive application was not established.\n研究产物核对 来源状态 来源核查 Last checked 2026-10-20\n源码、项目与 Demo 的核对依据 Original publication reviewed https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.12399  Author project page reviewed https://diamond-wm.github.io  Author-associated repository reviewed https://github.com/eloialonso/diamond  Repository license text inspected https://github.com/eloialonso/diamond/blob/main/LICENSE  Live artifact endpoint checked https://next.journee.ai/demo00001  Survey authors’ official resource mapping https://github.com/Eurekaleo/awesome-ai-for-games/blob/main/data/official-resources.json ","Conference paper cited as reference [9] in AI for Games in the Foundation Model Era. In Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems, 2024.","Eloi Alonso, Adam Jelley, Vincent Micheli, Anssi Kanervisto, Amos Storkey, Tim Pearce, and François Fleuret","In Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems, 2024.",[514,601],[625,2662,1787,560],"https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.12399","https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.12399","2405.12399","10.48550/arxiv.2405.12399",[8599],[8595,8596],[8591,8592,8593,8594],{"_532":1805,"_534":8567,"_536":8568,"_538":8569,"_540":614,"_541":542,"_543":8570,"_545":8571},[8588],[8587],[8583],[8573,8574,8575,8576,8577,8578],[8572,5081,5560],"MIT-licensed source and pretrained playable Atari/CS:GO world models are linked. Local interaction needs Python/model dependencies and a CUDA GPU; the project rep